<%# The model and the thinking level this session runs on, under the field
    the reader types in. Both are per-session choices, and both are the kind
    of thing that changes right before a prompt is sent — so they sit under
    the composer rather than in a settings page, the same width and centring
    as the box above them.

    Both lists hold real choices only. There is no "follow the default" entry:
    the default belongs to the persona, chosen where the persona is edited,
    and a picker that can say "default" hides the very thing the reader wants
    to know — which model, which effort.

    A change posts at once (there is no save button to forget), and the answer
    is this same row again with the new choice marked: a page cannot drift
    from what the session really runs on. -%>
<form id="session-settings" class="session-settings"
      data-model="<%= h(session_model) %>"
      data-thinking="<%= h(session_thinking) %>"
      hx-post="/s/<%= h(session_id) %>/settings<%= h(token_query) %>"
      hx-trigger="change from:select"
      hx-target="this"
      hx-swap="outerHTML">
  <label class="session-setting session-setting-model">
    <span class="session-setting-label">model</span>
    <select class="session-select" name="model" autocomplete="off"
            aria-label="Model sesi ini">
      <% model_choices.each do |choice| %>
        <option value="<%= h(choice[:value]) %>"<%= " selected" if choice[:value] == session_model %>><%= h(choice[:label]) %></option>
      <% end %>
      <%# The list is built from config and the provider catalog, and the model
          the session runs on can be a third thing (a hand-edited config, a
          catalog that failed to load). Showing the real one beats showing an
          empty box that misrepresents it. -%>
      <% unless session_model.empty? || model_choices.any? { |choice| choice[:value] == session_model } %>
        <option value="<%= h(session_model) %>" selected><%= h(session_model) %></option>
      <% end %>
    </select>
  </label>
  <label class="session-setting session-setting-thinking">
    <span class="session-setting-label">thinking</span>
    <select class="session-select" name="thinking" autocomplete="off"
            aria-label="Level thinking sesi ini">
      <% Persona::THINKING_LEVELS.each do |level| %>
        <option value="<%= h(level) %>"<%= " selected" if level == session_thinking %>><%= h(level) %></option>
      <% end %>
    </select>
  </label>
</form>
